    "result_text": "There is exactly one test class (`AcceptanceTest`) with the two owner-segment tests, and both pass. The build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ownerSegment` field, formatted `<TIER>_<AREA>`, on the owner response.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/java/.../util/OwnerSegment.java`** (new) \u2014 a small derivation util matching the repo's `Locality`/`MembershipLevel`/`CustomerCode` style:\n   - TIER = `PREMIUM` when `membershipLevel >= 3`, else `STANDARD`.\n   - AREA = `METRO` when the locality is a known region (`NSW`, `VIC`, `QLD`), else `REGIONAL`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added an `ownerSegment` MapStruct mapping. It feeds `OwnerSegment.of(...)` the effective membership level (the stored value, or the computed `MembershipLevel.level(points(...))` fallback \u2014 identical to the existing `membershipLevel` mapping) and the locality region (`CustomerCode.region(owner.getCustomerCode())` \u2014 the same source as the existing `locality` field, keeping the two consistent).\n\n3. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `ownerSegment` string property to the owner schema so it appears in the generated `OwnerDto` and the JSON response. Kept it a plain string (like `locality`) rather than an enum, since the mapper expression assigns a `String`.\n\n**Verification:** `AcceptanceTest.coreSegmentForKnownRegion` (Sydney/NSW, level 2 \u2192 `STANDARD_METRO`) and `functionalitySegmentForUnknownRegion` (random city \u2192 `STANDARD_REGIONAL`) both pass; full suite is `BUILD SUCCESS`, 0 failures.",
